1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,227
Spin a bicycle wheel as fast as you like.

2
00:00:03,227 --> 00:00:05,398
How high can the tyre valve go?

3
00:00:05,798 --> 00:00:08,525
Above the hub, never more than one radius.

4
00:00:08,525 --> 00:00:11,541
Below the hub, never more
than one radius down.

5
00:00:11,941 --> 00:00:15,333
Aarav checked this with a
measuring tape on his front wheel.

6
00:00:15,683 --> 00:00:20,115
However hard he spun it, the height
stayed between minus one radius and

7
00:00:20,115 --> 00:00:21,331
plus one radius.

8
00:00:21,831 --> 00:00:24,956
In maths, that limit is
called the range of sine.

9
00:00:24,956 --> 00:00:28,026
Today, the domain and
range of all six functions.

10
00:00:28,676 --> 00:00:30,906
Two words from the functions chapter.

11
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:34,087
The domain is every input
you are allowed to put in.

12
00:00:34,487 --> 00:00:37,540
The range is every output
that actually comes out.

13
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:42,366
Now let P go round the unit circle,
and track sine theta on a meter.

14
00:00:42,766 --> 00:00:45,025
Sine theta is the height of P.

15
00:00:45,025 --> 00:00:47,543
It climbs to one at ninety degrees.

16
00:00:47,943 --> 00:00:51,754
It falls to minus one at two
hundred and seventy degrees.

17
00:00:52,154 --> 00:00:55,944
P keeps going round and round,
but the height only repeats.

18
00:00:55,944 --> 00:00:58,901
It never goes above
one, or below minus one.

19
00:00:59,551 --> 00:01:01,629
Here is the proof, in four steps.

20
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:02,879
Step one.

21
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:05,311
P is on a circle of radius one.

22
00:01:05,311 --> 00:01:09,600
So its x and its y are never
more than one away from zero.

23
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:11,250
Step two.

24
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:16,237
So cosine theta lies from minus
one to one, and so does sine theta.

25
00:01:16,987 --> 00:01:17,941
Step three.

26
00:01:17,941 --> 00:01:22,362
Every real number theta, positive
or negative, gives a point P.

27
00:01:22,362 --> 00:01:26,056
So the domain of sine and
cosine is all real numbers.

28
00:01:26,806 --> 00:01:27,706
Step four.

29
00:01:27,631 --> 00:01:30,560
Every height from minus
one to one is reached.

30
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:34,571
So the range of both is the
closed interval, minus one to one.

31
00:01:35,221 --> 00:01:36,934
Tangent is different.

32
00:01:36,934 --> 00:01:40,857
Tangent theta is sine theta
divided by cosine theta.

33
00:01:41,257 --> 00:01:44,159
Let theta creep up towards ninety degrees.

34
00:01:44,159 --> 00:01:46,139
Cosine shrinks towards zero.

35
00:01:46,539 --> 00:01:48,112
And tangent shoots up.

36
00:01:48,112 --> 00:01:52,674
Five point six, eleven, fifty seven,
five hundred and seventy three.

37
00:01:53,074 --> 00:01:58,601
At exactly ninety degrees, cosine is
zero, and we can never divide by zero.

38
00:01:58,601 --> 00:02:00,794
Tangent is not defined there.

39
00:02:01,444 --> 00:02:05,209
Cosine is zero at every
odd multiple of pi by two.

40
00:02:05,209 --> 00:02:09,405
So tangent's domain is all real
numbers except those points.

41
00:02:09,405 --> 00:02:12,022
But its range is all real numbers.

42
00:02:12,772 --> 00:02:17,063
Secant is one over cosine, so it
skips the same points as tangent.

43
00:02:17,463 --> 00:02:20,268
Cosine is never bigger than one in size.

44
00:02:20,268 --> 00:02:23,926
So one over cosine is never
smaller than one in size.

45
00:02:23,926 --> 00:02:27,214
Secant is at least one,
or at most minus one.

46
00:02:27,864 --> 00:02:30,698
Cosecant and cotangent
have sine underneath.

47
00:02:30,698 --> 00:02:34,228
They skip every multiple
of pi, where sine is zero.

48
00:02:34,878 --> 00:02:36,002
Side by side.

49
00:02:36,002 --> 00:02:40,715
Sine accepts every real number, but
its range is small, only minus one

50
00:02:40,715 --> 00:02:41,615
to one.

51
00:02:41,864 --> 00:02:43,992
Tangent is the other way round.

52
00:02:43,992 --> 00:02:47,744
Its domain has gaps, but its
range is every real number.

53
00:02:48,344 --> 00:02:49,472
Now you try.

54
00:02:49,472 --> 00:02:52,462
Can sine theta ever equal one point two?

55
00:02:52,462 --> 00:02:53,865
Pause and decide.

56
00:02:57,065 --> 00:02:57,965
No!

57
00:02:57,535 --> 00:03:02,248
One point two is more than one, and
sine theta is a height on a circle

58
00:03:02,248 --> 00:03:03,404
of radius one.

59
00:03:04,054 --> 00:03:05,116
Remember this.

60
00:03:05,116 --> 00:03:09,615
Sine and cosine take any angle, but
their answers stay between minus one

61
00:03:09,615 --> 00:03:10,515
and one.

62
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,021
Quick one.

63
00:03:12,021 --> 00:03:14,799
Is tangent defined at theta equals pi?

64
00:03:14,799 --> 00:03:16,129
Pause and think.

65
00:03:19,329 --> 00:03:20,229
Yes!

66
00:03:19,911 --> 00:03:22,672
Cosine pi is minus one, not zero.

67
00:03:22,672 --> 00:03:24,555
So tangent pi is zero.

68
00:03:24,555 --> 00:03:28,263
Only the odd multiples
of pi by two are missing.

69
00:03:28,913 --> 00:03:30,649
Now, one worked example.

70
00:03:30,999 --> 00:03:33,812
Find the range of three
plus two sine theta.

71
00:03:34,312 --> 00:03:35,212
Step one.

72
00:03:35,212 --> 00:03:38,097
Sine theta lies from minus one to one.

73
00:03:38,847 --> 00:03:39,778
Step two.

74
00:03:39,778 --> 00:03:41,175
Multiply by two.

75
00:03:41,175 --> 00:03:44,458
Two sine theta lies from minus two to two.

76
00:03:45,208 --> 00:03:46,205
Step three.

77
00:03:46,205 --> 00:03:47,148
Add three.

78
00:03:47,148 --> 00:03:50,669
Three plus two sine theta
lies from one to five.

79
00:03:51,419 --> 00:03:53,414
So the range is one to five.

80
00:03:53,414 --> 00:03:56,284
The wave is squeezed
between those two lines.

81
00:03:56,934 --> 00:03:58,400
Now, the exam trap.

82
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:03,208
Many students think: cosine lies
from minus one to one, so secant does

83
00:04:03,208 --> 00:04:04,108
too.

84
00:04:04,109 --> 00:04:07,155
But one over a small
number is a big number.

85
00:04:07,155 --> 00:04:09,930
When cosine is one half, secant is two.

86
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:13,365
Secant never lies strictly
between minus one and one.

87
00:04:14,014 --> 00:04:15,634
Where is this asked?

88
00:04:15,634 --> 00:04:20,690
In PUC exams and in JEE Main: find
the range of an expression built from

89
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:22,027
sine and cosine.

90
00:04:22,627 --> 00:04:23,818
Exam level now.

91
00:04:23,818 --> 00:04:27,301
How many integers are in
the range of this function?

92
00:04:27,301 --> 00:04:28,543
Pause and solve.

93
00:04:33,943 --> 00:04:35,175
The answer is B.

94
00:04:35,175 --> 00:04:36,075
Nine.

95
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:40,517
Sine theta lies from minus one
to one, and it reaches both ends.

96
00:04:41,017 --> 00:04:42,479
Multiply by four.

97
00:04:42,479 --> 00:04:45,951
Four sine theta lies
from minus four to four.

98
00:04:46,451 --> 00:04:47,616
Subtract three.

99
00:04:47,616 --> 00:04:50,559
The function lies from minus seven to one.

100
00:04:51,059 --> 00:04:54,418
The integers from minus
seven to one are nine in all.

101
00:04:55,018 --> 00:04:56,480
Here is your recap.

102
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,983
Screenshot this card.

103
00:05:01,183 --> 00:05:04,020
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

104
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,320
One.

105
00:05:04,945 --> 00:05:07,386
What is the range of cosine theta?

106
00:05:08,286 --> 00:05:09,186
Two.

107
00:05:08,858 --> 00:05:12,600
Name two angles where
tangent theta is not defined.

108
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:14,400
Three.

109
00:05:14,198 --> 00:05:16,726
Can secant theta equal one half?

110
00:05:16,726 --> 00:05:17,626
Why not?

111
00:05:18,707 --> 00:05:22,720
Next time: trace the valve's height
over time, and a wave appears.

112
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:25,661
We draw the graphs of
sine, cosine and tangent.
